---
// The residency angle, written as the awkward part rather than the easy
// part.
//
// That every unit clears AED 2 million is true and takes one sentence. The
// page worth writing is about the sentence after it: this is an off-plan
// purchase with a 2030 handover, and the threshold is where that question
// starts rather than ends. The hub can say so because it also carries the
// visas section; the product site has to sell the flat.
import VerticalLayout from "../../layouts/VerticalLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "@dst/ui/PageHero.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
import Faq from "@dst/ui/Faq.astro";

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: "Does a Palm Central apartment qualify for the Dubai Golden Visa?",
    a: "Every unit type is priced above the <strong>AED 2 million</strong> property threshold, the cheapest by AED 700,000. Clearing the threshold is the entry condition, not the whole test — an off-plan purchase raises questions a completed, unmortgaged property does not.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long is the visa?",
    a: "It depends which official source you read, and both are current: the UAE government platform's category table gives ten years for public investments and five for real estate, while the Dubai Land Department's own investor service gives a ten-year renewable permit for property worth AED 2 million or more. Ask the authority processing the file.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can I apply before handover?",
    a: "That is the question to put to the Land Department rather than to a sales office. Off-plan status and mortgaged value are treated differently from a completed property, and handover here is <strong>September 2030</strong>.",
  },
  {
    q: "Could the threshold change before then?",
    a: "It could. Thresholds and criteria are set federally and have moved before; four years is long enough for them to move again, in either direction. A purchase made only for the visa is a purchase exposed to that.",
  },
];
---
<VerticalLayout
  vertical="palm-central"
  current="/palm-central/golden-visa/"
  prose
  title="Palm Central and the Dubai Golden Visa threshold"
  description="Every Palm Central unit in Dubai clears the AED 2 million property threshold, the cheapest by AED 700,000. The harder question is what an off-plan purchase with a 2030 handover does about it."
  image="/covers/pc-visa.jpg"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Golden Visa"
    title="Palm Central and the Dubai Golden Visa threshold"
    image="/covers/pc-visa.jpg"
    imageAlt="Cut-paper illustration: a low horizontal ledge with three flat cream blocks of differing heights standing on it."
    imageKind="generated"
  >
    <p class="lede">
      The easy half is settled: at <strong>AED 2.7 million</strong> the
      cheapest Palm Central apartment clears the
      <strong>AED 2 million</strong> property threshold by
      <strong>AED 700,000</strong>, and every larger unit clears it further.
      The half that matters is what happens between now and
      <strong>September 2030</strong>.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Where each unit sits</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Unit</th><th>From</th><th>Above AED 2M by</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>1-bedroom apartment</td><td>AED 2.7M</td><td>AED 0.7M</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2-bedroom apartment</td><td>AED 4.3M</td><td>AED 2.3M</td></tr>
        <tr><td>3-bedroom apartment</td><td>AED 7.5M</td><td>AED 5.5M</td></tr>
        <tr><td>4-bedroom apartment</td><td>AED 12.4M</td><td>AED 10.4M</td></tr>
        <tr><td>4–5-bedroom townhouse</td><td>AED 14.9M</td><td>AED 12.9M</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Note what the first row means in practice. A margin of AED 700,000 is
      comfortable against the threshold as it stands, and it is also the
      row with the least room if the threshold ever moves up. The larger
      units are not only bigger purchases; they are less exposed ones.
    </p>

    <h2>Off-plan is the complication</h2>
    <p>
      A Golden Visa granted on property is granted on a property that exists
      and is owned. An off-plan purchase is a contract to buy one. Whether,
      and at what point, the route opens on a purchase like this is decided
      by the processing authority and turns on things a brochure will not
      settle: the registered value, whether the purchase is mortgaged, and
      what stage the build has reached. None of those is a reason not to
      buy. All of them are reasons not to treat the visa as included.
    </p>

    <h2>Four years is a long exposure</h2>
    <p>
      Between booking and handover sits about four years of federal policy.
      The threshold has been at AED 2 million for some time, and the two
      official sources currently disagree about whether the permit runs five
      years or ten — which is itself a reminder that this is an
      administered scheme rather than a fixed right. Buy the flat because
      the flat is worth it; count the residency as a benefit to confirm
      rather than a term of the deal.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Callout kind="warn">
    <p>
      Thresholds, eligibility and permit lengths are set by UAE federal
      authorities and can change. Nothing on this page is an assurance that
      a purchase at Palm Central will result in a visa. Confirm the current
      requirements with the authority that will process the application
      before treating any purchase as a residency route.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Next</h2>
    <p>
      The mechanics of the property route, the fees in full and the
      disagreement between the two official sources are on
      <a href="/visas/golden/" title="Golden Visa in Dubai through property investment">the Golden Visa page</a>,
      with the property-specific conditions on
      <a href="/visas/properties/" title="Which Dubai property qualifies for a Golden Visa">the qualifying-property page</a>.
      What is actually being bought is on
      <a href="/palm-central/prices/" title="Palm Central prices in Dubai">the prices page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Faq items={faqItems} />

  <section class="container">
    <p class="source-note">
      Unit prices: The National, 24 June 2026; handover September 2030. The
      AED 2 million threshold, the ten-year renewable investor permit and
      the federal category table: Dubai Land Department and the UAE
      government platform, as set out on this site's
      <a href="/visas/golden/" title="Golden Visa in Dubai">Golden Visa page</a>,
      read 22 September 2026. Margins above the threshold are arithmetic.
      Nothing here is immigration or investment advice.
    </p>
  </section>
</VerticalLayout>
